WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:07.337
First: an Attack Surface Reduction policy
in Intune is assigned to a user group.

3
00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:08.350
What happens?

4
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.575
The answer is b.

5
00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:12.961
It never applies, because
Microsoft Learn says Defender

6
00:00:12.961 --> 00:00:16.275
for Endpoint management
supports device objects only.

7
00:00:16.275 --> 00:00:18.375
Assign it to an Entra device group.

8
00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:21.979
Second: a G C C High S O C
connects to Graph without the

9
00:00:21.979 --> 00:00:26.613
environment parameter and lists
incidents, and the list is empty.

10
00:00:26.613 --> 00:00:28.226
What's the most likely reason?

11
00:00:28.226 --> 00:00:29.450
The answer is b.

12
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:32.121
The session read the
worldwide host instead of

13
00:00:32.121 --> 00:00:34.449
the tenant's own cloud;
connect with U S Gov.

14
00:00:34.449 --> 00:00:37.462
A missing role would have
produced an error naming it.

15
00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:41.787
An empty list with no error is exactly
the danger the guide warns about.

16
00:00:41.787 --> 00:00:46.750
The module page has three more questions,
each linked to the unit that answers it.
